    "2. Use GET only: GET /calendar reads the sources, GET /calendar/tasks reads your tasks, GET /calendar/task-proposals reads the tasks waiting for review, and GET /calendar/connections reads the calendars you can choose. A read may answer in keep the starting list definitions a first read finds missing; keep them where you keep your lists.",
    "3. Changing tasks, proposals, dates or calendar choices is not done through this route (a POST answers 405): it is workflow:keep-my-calendar-tasks-and-proposals, which keeps them in your own store."
